full.said:
gate 1b's C lexer reads a preprocessing directive where the pinned GCC does not (closure cell U+00A0 between a backslash and the line end in a line comment, 'int a;
// c\\xa0
#define FOO
#ifdef FOO
int b;
#endif
int z;
'): its directive readers keep ('a', 'z') and the pinned GCC 14.3 at -std=gnu99 keeps ('a', 'b', 'z'), so an arm one of them grades is an arm the other compiles, or drops

